    caution: "Thorns can cause puncture wounds. Wear gloves and eye protection when tying or pruning long stems.", about: "Rosa is a large genus and garden roses combine many species into climbers, ramblers, shrubs, floribundas and hybrid teas. Flowering on old or current growth varies by group, making a cultivar or at least growth-class identification genuinely useful. For now, observation of flower form, hips, repeat pattern and cane habit should guide the record.", provenance: "Genus and trained garden-rose status are secure; cultivar and rose class need a clear flowering record or original label.", family: "Rosaceae", genus: "Rosa", foliage: "Deciduous; compound leaves", habit: "Supported shrub or climber", role: "Wall-trained summer flower through the centre of Bed 5", observation: "The plant is tied to support and flowers from summer into early autumn.", status: "Photograph flower face, buds, hips and full cane habit to narrow the cultivar or at least its pruning class.", source: RHS.roses,
