    description: "This newly planted Echeveria forms a large symmetrical rosette of broad, fleshy leaves covered in a powdery grey-purple bloom, with a fine pink edge catching the light. The photographs most closely fit ‘Perle von Nürnberg’, but several related hybrids can look nearly identical without a retained label or flowers, so the cultivar remains an explicit working assumption. It suits the Stone Bed’s sun and sharp drainage through summer, but unlike the hardy houseleeks beside it, it will not survive a Bromsgrove winter outdoors.",
